  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2020) position from NRB Commercial Bank's own audited annual report multi-year key-financial table, taken from the FY2020 report (the reporting year's own document). Basis note: this year is on a SOLO basis. The FY2015-FY2019 tables that supply the earlier years of this series are consolidated, a 0.12% difference at FY2018; the basis changes at FY2020. Off-balance-sheet trap: the FY2022 report's summary table prints FY2018 total assets as 86,598.12, which is that year's balance-sheet total (67,142.86) plus its off-balance-sheet items (19,455.25) — the sum is exact. Its FY2019 and later columns exclude off-balance-sheet items. This dataset never sources FY2018 total assets from that report. The FY2021 report is excluded entirely: its only extractable table is a horizontal analysis in which every value is a percentage of a base year, so it carries no usable figures at all. Calculated line item(s): total_capital. total_capital, where derived, is this report's own Tier-I plus Tier-II rather than a later report's total, so the capital stack stays internally consistent. car_pct, where derived, is total capital over risk-weighted assets. classified_loans, where derived, is the reported ratio applied to reported loans and advances. GAP-FILL -- the FY2020 report does not print 4 row(s), taken from the nearest report that does: investments_securities from AR2022, total_operating_income from AR2023, tax_expense from AR2022, required_capital from AR2023. Total assets are never gap-filled, to keep the off-balance-sheet-inflated columns out of the series. RESTATEMENTS -- 1 figure(s) here differ in other NRBC reports; the contemporaneous value is kept: total_deposits: this record uses 90177.3 (AR2020); AR2022/AR2024 report 95311.1.",
